      "side": 1,
      "message": "I believe you\u0027re aware but just in case: the placement choice here has subtle consequences. --log_level support is added for `wpr record` and `wpr replay` but not `wpr installroot` or `wpr removeroot`. The last 2 use CertConfig, which does not reuse CommonConfig (the \"Common\" in  `CommonConfig` is quite misleading in that sense...)\n\nThis is even reflected in the CheckArgs modifications. There are 3 CheckArgs methods in this file:\n1. for CommonConfig -\u003e you added a SetLogLevel() call\n2. for RecordCommand (L375) -\u003e it calls (1), so it calls SetLogLevel()\n3. for CertConfig (L197) -\u003e it does not call SetLogLevel()\n\nNot having --log_level for installroot and removeroot is probably fine, since:\na) the default log level is INFO, so it\u0027s not like we\u0027re omitting any useful information from the user\nb) those 2 commands are short-lived anyways\n\nOne request I have is that you rename the (1) and (2) to CheckArgsAndSetLogLevel(), to reflect they have a side-effect now",
      "revId": "3cf2bff32d9022e787e2a386e8c789616bb84f45",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
